{"aligned_passages":[{"anchor":"consequence-theorems","mapping_field":"claim_ids","mapping_ref":"sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json","paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7","passage_ref":"sha256:1fd49f692320db9f27935d8a5c8bc9bc22bddf38904cfd9fa8def31510d242d5/papers/long.md/sha256:a6adce2af176e8100e5f874b46c0da40fde53f56940f925c820d53da0079f829/papers/long.json/passages/consequence-theorems","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&paper=long&passage=consequence-theorems","span":{"end_byte":213512,"end_line":2401,"start_byte":190942,"start_line":2062},"stage":"long"}],"lenses":{"consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c3&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257bm-c3&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&node=long.record-257bm-c3&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&view=arguments&node=long.record-257bm-c3&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=bb1e0df1c0a23087463e72ce0bd0db12f00c6bb5ce16d74195c581ead3dd0ce7&ref=sha256%3A72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696%2Fnodes%2Flong.record-257bm-c3","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"The evidence mapping records a Lean proof of exactly this statement. Lean status per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c3"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c3"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c3","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.69 (A compatible family of finite supports)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.69, p. 64, label record:257bm-c3","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $b_{n,d}\\in\\{0,1\\}$ satisfy $b_{n+1,d}=b_{n,d}$ whenever $2d\\le n$. Define\n$$\nE_n=\\{d:2\\le d\\le n,\\ b_{n,d}=1\\},\\qquad\n D_n=E_n\\cap\\{2,\\ldots,\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor\\}.\n$$\nThe four conditions on the finite rows, required for every $n\\ge2$, are\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n 2^{\\max\\{c_{D_n}(n)-1,0\\}}-1&\\le S(D_n,1,n-1),\\\\\n \\sum_{\\substack{d\\in E_n\\\\d>\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor}}2^{n-d}\n     &=H(D_n,1,n),\\\\\n H(D_n,1,n)&<2^{n-\\lfloor n/2\\rfloor},\\\\\n Q(E_n,n)&=2^{n-1}-1.\n \\end{aligned}\n$$\nThe first condition implies that the integer in the next two lines is nonnegative. The second specifies the binary value of the upper half of the row, the third bounds that value by its available number of bits, and the fourth is the exact quotient equation. The maximum in the first line records natural-number subtraction at the case $c_{D_n}(n)=0$.*\n\n*These are the finite hypotheses of the compatible-limit construction. The bit condition fixes coordinate $d$ from row $2d$ onward. Unlike the independent finite supports in Definition 6.66, the rows therefore have a prescribed common limit. This extra structure is not, by itself, a proof of strictness between the corresponding existence statements.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c3","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c3","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_bit_stable%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_bit_stable%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_bit_stable"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c3","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_finite_row_conditions%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_finite_row_conditions%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_finite_row_conditions"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257bm-c3","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_first_condition_gives_nonneg%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c3%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_compatible_first_condition_gives_nonneg%22%2C%22formal